---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Kitchen Confidence — Rabbit Hole" description="Making cooking fun and accessible through community, AI, and open data">
  <section class="hero-case">
    <a href="/rabbit-holes/" class="back-link">← Rabbit Holes</a>
    <div class="case-tenets">
      <a href="/clarity/" class="tenet-link">Clarity Tenet</a>
      <a href="/insight/" class="tenet-link secondary">Insight Tenet</a>
    </div>
    <h1>Kitchen Confidence</h1>
    <p class="case-tagline">Making cooking fun and accessible for families through community, AI, and open data</p>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-label">The Problem This Solves</h2>
    <div class="case-content">
      <div class="problem-grid">
        <div class="problem-card">
          <span class="problem-quote">"Cooking classes cost £100+ per session — who can afford that?"</span>
        </div>
        <div class="problem-card">
          <span class="problem-quote">"YouTube is one-way. I can't ask questions when I'm stuck"</span>
        </div>
        <div class="problem-card">
          <span class="problem-quote">"No home economics in schools. Where do I even start?"</span>
        </div>
        <div class="problem-card">
          <span class="problem-quote">"I'm bored of what I cook — stuck in a rut"</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        Cooking is one of the most essential life skills — yet traditional ways of learning have disappeared.
        <strong>We don't hang out with grandma anymore.</strong> Classes are expensive.
        Cookbooks are intimidating. YouTube doesn't answer back.
      </p>
      <p>
        The result? A generation of capable adults who feel <strong>intimidated in their own kitchens</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-label">The Methodology</h2>
    <div class="case-content">
      <p class="vision-statement">
        <strong>Everyone can be a cook. Everyone is a teacher.</strong><br/>
        The future of food is community + AI + accessible data.
      </p>
      
      <div class="method-steps">
        
        <div class="method-step">
          <div class="step-number">1</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h3>Community as Teacher</h3>
            <p>Like ADPList for design, but for cooking. Everyone who's made a hot meal has something to share. Pair experienced home cooks with beginners via live video.</p>
            <p class="client-application"><strong>For clients:</strong> User-generated expertise reduces support costs while building loyalty.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="method-step">
          <div class="step-number">2</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h3>AI as Sous-Chef</h3>
            <p>Not replacing cooks — enhancing them. AI that knows your allergies, suggests ingredient swaps, and converts recipes for different household sizes.</p>
            <p class="client-application"><strong>For clients:</strong> Personalisation without scale problems. The AI handles edge cases humans can't remember.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="method-step">
          <div class="step-number">3</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h3>Data as Democratiser</h3>
            <p>Hidden APIs in supermarket websites contain structured product data — prices, nutrition, availability. Extract it; don't OCR brochure PDFs.</p>
            <p class="client-application"><strong>For clients:</strong> "Talk to the kitchen, not read the menu." Real-time data beats scraped screenshots.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="method-step">
          <div class="step-number">4</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h3>Tactile as Therapy</h3>
            <p><strong>Breaditation:</strong> Mindfulness through bread-making. Tested at a college where students weren't showing up. Got them elbows-deep in dough. Parents overjoyed with fresh loaves.</p>
            <p class="client-application"><strong>For clients:</strong> Physical creation beats digital consumption. Sometimes the best engagement is offline.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="method-step">
          <div class="step-number">5</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h3>Nostalgia as Hook</h3>
            <p>The Generation Game skit: Turn Aldi's famous middle aisle into a gameshow. QR codes, memory challenges, tongue-in-cheek humour. See working example below.</p>
            <p class="client-application"><strong>For clients:</strong> Cultural memory is an untapped marketing asset. 30 years of shared context = instant emotional connection.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section video-section">
    <h2 class="section-label">Spoof Ad Campaign: The Generation Game</h2>
    <div class="case-content">
      <p>
        What if Aldi's legendary middle aisle became a gameshow? This spoof ad concept turns the UK's beloved 
        <em>Generation Game</em> conveyor belt into an interactive shopping experience.
      </p>
      
      <div class="video-container">
        <video controls poster="/videos/aldi-generation-game-poster.jpg">
          <source src="/videos/aldi-generation-game.mp4" type="video/mp4">
          Your browser does not support the video tag.
        </video>
      </div>
      
      <div class="video-concept">
        <h3>The Concept</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Format:</strong> 30-second ads airing in commercial breaks</li>
          <li><strong>Mechanic:</strong> Products scroll past on a conveyor belt</li>
          <li><strong>Interaction:</strong> QR code links to form — viewers enter products they remember</li>
          <li><strong>Host:</strong> German comedian popular in the UK (think Henning Wehn energy)</li>
          <li><strong>Tone:</strong> Nostalgic, tongue-in-cheek, self-aware</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      
      <div class="insight-box">
        <p><strong>The Business Insight:</strong></p>
        <p>This isn't just entertainment — it's <strong>attention engineering</strong>. 
        Viewers who play along are 10x more likely to visit the store that week. 
        The nostalgia hook (Generation Game ran 1971-2002) targets the exact demographic 
        with disposable income: 40-65 year olds.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-label">Key Technical Insights</h2>
    <div class="case-content">
      <div class="vision-grid">
        <div class="vision-card">
          <h4>Pantry Tetris Algorithm</h4>
          <p>Zero-waste ingredient reuse. If Week 1 uses half a celery bunch, Week 2 recipes automatically include the rest.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="vision-card">
          <h4>The Peloton Model</h4>
          <p>Live instruction + community accountability + budget logistics. Subscription cooking that actually works.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="vision-card">
          <h4>Hidden API Discovery</h4>
          <p>Intercept `window.__INITIAL_STATE__` from supermarket websites. Structured JSON beats PDF scraping every time.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="vision-card">
          <h4>Voice-Controlled VOD</h4>
          <p>DJI Osmo Action 4 streams RTMP. Videos pause at each step until user says "Ready." Hands stay clean.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-label">When to Use This Methodology</h2>
    <div class="case-content">
      <ul class="use-cases">
        <li><strong>Subscription platforms</strong> needing retention through multi-modality (read + watch + do)</li>
        <li><strong>Community businesses</strong> where users can teach each other</li>
        <li><strong>DTC brands</strong> wanting to turn content into interactive experiences</li>
        <li><strong>Educational platforms</strong> where tactile/live engagement beats passive consumption</li>
        <li><strong>Brands with nostalgia assets</strong> — cultural memory is untapped marketing gold</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-label">Related</h2>
    <div class="related-items">
      <a href="/rabbit-holes/signal-from-noise/" class="related-link">
        <span class="related-icon">📊</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Signal from Noise</strong>
          <span>Turning overwhelming content into accessible insight</span>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a href="/play/the-15m-paradox/" class="related-link">
        <span class="related-icon">📻</span>
        <div>
          <strong>The £15M Paradox</strong>
          <span>When "loss-making" ventures are strategic gold</span>
        </div>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section cta-section">
    <h2>Want to make your product more engaging?</h2>
    <p>Let's talk about community, nostalgia, and the tactics that create loyalty.</p>
    <a href="mailto:dave@wordandmouth.com" class="cta-button">Start a Conversation</a>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero-case {
    padding: 10rem 2rem 4rem;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  
  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }
  
  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  
  .case-tenets {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .tenet-link {
    background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.15);
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  
  .tenet-link.secondary {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  
  .hero-case h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  
  .case-tagline {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  
  .case-content {
    max-width: 700px;
  }
  
  .case-content p {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  
  .case-content strong {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  
  .vision-statement {
    font-size: 1.4rem !important;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem !important;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  
  .problem-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  
  .problem-card {
    background: #111;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
  }
  
  .problem-quote {
    font-style: italic;
    color: #ccc;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  
  .method-steps {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  
  .method-step {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  
  .step-number {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent);
    line-height: 1;
    min-width: 2rem;
  }
  
  .step-content h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  
  .step-content p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1rem !important;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem !important;
  }
  
  .client-application {
    background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.1);
    padding: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem !important;
    color: #ccc !important;
  }
  
  .video-section {
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.03));
  }
  
  .video-container {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #000;
  }
  
  .video-container video {
    width: 100%;
    display: block;
  }
  
  .video-concept {
    background: #111;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  
  .video-concept h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  
  .video-concept ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }
  
  .video-concept li {
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #ccc;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  
  .video-concept li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  
  .insight-box {
    background: #111;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  
  .insight-box p {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem !important;
  }
  
  .insight-box p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0 !important;
    color: var(--muted) !important;
  }
  
  .vision-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  
  .vision-card {
    background: #111;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }
  
  .vision-card h4 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  
  .vision-card p {
    font-size: 0.9rem !important;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 0 !important;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  
  .use-cases {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }
  
  .use-cases li {
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  
  .use-cases li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  
  .related-items {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  
  .related-link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    background: #111;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }
  
  .related-link:hover {
    border-left-color: var(--accent);
  }
  
  .related-icon {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }
  
  .related-link strong {
    display: block;
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  
  .related-link span {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  
  .cta-section {
    text-align: center;
  }
  
  .cta-section h2 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .cta-section p {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .problem-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    
    .vision-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    
    .method-step {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.75rem;
    }
  }
</style>
